## Pull request overview

Copilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.




<details>
<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>

**src/test/app/AMMClawbackMPT_test.cpp:1962**
* PR description/test plan says the new rounding-to-zero scenario is tested under three amendment combinations (including fixAMMClawbackRounding off), but run() only exercises fixCleanup3_4_0 on/off while always enabling fixAMMClawbackRounding via `all`. Either update the PR description/test plan to match what’s actually covered, or add the missing fixAMMClawbackRounding-off coverage with the correct expectations.
```
        FeatureBitset const all{jtx::testableAmendments() | fixAMMClawbackRounding};

        testInvalidRequest(all);
        testFeatureDisabled(all);
        testAMMClawbackAmount(all);
        testAMMClawbackAmount(all - fixCleanup3_4_0);
        testAMMClawbackAmountRoundsToZero(all);
        testAMMClawbackAmountRoundsToZero(all - fixCleanup3_4_0);
```
**src/libxrpl/tx/transactors/dex/AMMClawback.cpp:361**
* The error return here constructs the 4th tuple element (std::optional<STAmount>) from a default STAmount, which makes the optional engaged even though the TER is a failure. For clarity and consistency with other early returns in this function (which use std::nullopt on failures), return std::nullopt for the optional amount.
```
        if (rules.enabled(fixCleanup3_4_0) &&
            (amountRounded == beast::kZero || amount2Rounded == beast::kZero))
            return {tecAMM_FAILED, STAmount{}, STAmount{}, STAmount{}};
```
</details>

